# Reuse-first architecture — mandatory pre-coding gate

Before writing or editing any code, tests, scripts, configuration, or
infrastructure definition, read the canonical skill and complete its gate:

> Read `.agent-skills/reuse-first-architecture/SKILL.md` and its references
> before implementation.

The gate applies to every programming edit, even small or trivial ones:

- Search before building: reuse, adapt, extend, or build — naming the
  component inspected and the reason.
- Apply SOLID and dependency inversion: transport stays thin,
  `src/image_translation` never imports FastAPI/server code, model and
  tokenizer resolution stays centralized.
- Preserve public contracts, HTML/entity protection invariants, cache/
  offline/GPU/precision/language-pair policies, and `environment.yml` as
  the dependency source of truth.
- Implement one coherent slice, verify with the relevant tests, and
  report evidence. Do not claim a suite passed without running it.

This rule does not override `AGENTS.md` or more specific repository
instructions.
